Keep the archive's own live count private to the owner

live_counts() no longer returns the 'hub' row at all, so a visitor cannot read
it even by calling the API directly with the publishable key. The number comes
only from hub_viewers(token), which compares a SHA-256 hash held in owner_key
(RLS on, no policies, no grants).

The masthead chip appears only in a browser that arrived once at ?owner=<token>;
the token is stored locally and stripped from the URL so it never appears in the
address bar or a shared link. ?owner=off forgets it. The token is not in this
repo.

Badge counts for the archived sites stay public -- that is the point of the
badge -- and the scraped "people in these gallis right now" ticker is unchanged.

